  "step_1": "The decision reason is based on the skewness of the lotteries, specifically preferring the one that is more right-skewed (i.e., where a greater portion of the probability is assigned to unfavorable outcomes). To assess skewness in this context, we need to evaluate the distribution of outcomes relative to their probabilities. For Lottery A: -3000 with 90%, 0 with 10%. Most of the probability (90%) is on a non-zero loss, which is unfavorable, and only 10% chance of no loss. For Lottery B: -6000 with 45%, 0 with 55%. Here, the unfavorable outcome (-6000) has lower probability (45%) than the favorable one (0 with 55%). Thus, Lottery A assigns a much higher probability (90%) to a loss than Lottery B does to its larger loss (45%). Therefore, Lottery A is more right-skewed than Lottery B, because a larger portion of its probability mass is on an unfavorable outcome. According to the decision reason, Lottery A should be preferred because it is more right-skewed.",
